259
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,500
You haven't won at all.

260
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:10,975
What a waste of time.

261
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,110
Agumon!

262
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:22,900
TK, I'll come back
again, if you want me to.

263
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:29,210
Agumon!

264
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,360
What do you know?

265
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,441
It's a digi-egg.

266
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,521
Do you think it could be Angemon?

267
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:47,840
I know it is.

268
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:50,537
He's just resting for a
while to regain his strength.

269
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:51,557
But don't worry.

270
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,737
You'll see him again when he digi-falls.

271
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:56,900
I will make sure to take
really good care of him.

272
00:19:57,520 --> 00:20:00,300
You saved my life, Angemon. Huh?

273
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:03,625
Look, the island is coming
back together again.

274
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:04,910
Exactly.

275
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,357
Devamon's been defeated.

276
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:10,205
When evil is eliminated, the
island returns to its normal state.

277
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:14,820
With Devimon out of the
way, I can take over now.

278
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:17,557
Hello, you're forgetting about me?

279
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,760
Leomon, get me out of here!

280
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:22,320
Why can't the mad guys ever win?

281
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,597
What's with those other
evil Digimon across the sea?

282
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,157
Yeah, I thought we were going home.

283
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,480
I don't want to have to fight again.

284
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,568
Oh, I think I broke a nail.

285
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:36,677
Well, according to Leomon's
legend, we've got to do it.

286
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,231
Remember, he said we're the Digidestined.

287
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,254
Something's happening.

288
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,080
Ah, I've heard of you kids.

289
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,673
I must say I'm pleased.

290
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,900
Excuse me, sir. Tell us.

291
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,500
Who are you and what do you want?

292
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,877
See you

293
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:09,700
next time.

294
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:33,797
Please tell me, I'm just
going to see you right now.

295
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:37,800
It's not all that you can see.

296
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:43,540
It's cold, so it's cold.

297
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:46,737
I'm wearing a jacket with my hands.

298
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:49,180
I don't know if I like it.

299
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:51,580
It's a dream.

300
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:56,077
The future of the rain

301
00:21:56,160 --> 00:22:01,537
is I'll see

302
00:22:01,620 --> 00:22:03,940
you next time.

303
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,600
I wish you
